        "githubCommitAuthorName": "Radek Tobolka",
        "githubCommitAuthorEmail": "tobolka@gmail.com",
        "githubCommitMessage": "Keep reused race pages and series sign-ups off the wrong races\n\nTBC s\u00e9rie reshuffled its 2026 calendar and kept the race pages: zavod-211\nwent from T\u00e1bor on 25 Oct to Vimperk on 14 Nov. A shared URL plus\nplace-only titles that reduce to the series name scored as one race, so\nthe old T\u00e1bor row took Vimperk's name. A same URL no longer joins two\nraces weeks apart in two known, different places.\n\nThe series homepage's \"REGISTRACE 2026\" button (the season's points\nsign-up) became every round's entry link. On a page several races share,\nan entry link now counts only beside this race's name or date.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
