        "githubCommitAuthorName": "Radek Tobolka",
        "githubCommitAuthorEmail": "tobolka@gmail.com",
        "githubCommitMessage": "File the Swiss Bike Cup's road criterium as a road criterium.\n\nEvery stage of the \u0160koda Swiss Bike Cup was filed as XCO, because the\nadapter hardcoded the series' usual discipline instead of reading the line\nthe site prints under each stage title. So the GP Osterhas \u2014 a road\ncriterium on an 880 m circuit in Affoltern am Albis, where a road bike is\nmandatory from U17 and which is not even scored in the cup's overall\nclassification \u2014 sat in the catalogue as a cross-country race, and Leysin's\nshort track went unrecorded beside its XCO.\n\nThat line is also the only durable answer for the seasons to come: the\nhomepage lists whatever stages the current season has, so next year's\nrounds arrive through the same seven-slug shape and inherit whatever the\nadapter assumes. Read the label instead of assuming.\n\nThe same applied to the audience, decided by matching the place name\n\"Mol\u00e9son\" \u2014 right for 2026, where that round happens to be the series'\nfirst kids-only stage, and wrong the moment the kids round moves. Take it\nfr",
